{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"frank-rocky-rat","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Defect\n\nEpic `6ed2-9cbd-9a2a-4ff0` (\"merge the held-out twin test modules\") closed on the strength of an\nacceptance criterion that measured the wrong set. Its AC1 glob was:\n\n    git ls-files 'tests/**/test_*_heldout.py'\n\nwhich returns **0 rows** at `origin/main`. The epic was therefore reported complete.\n\nSix held-out modules are still in the tree. They are invisible to that glob because they end in\n`_heldout_<4-hex-quad>.py`, not `_heldout.py`:\n\n| created | LOC | module |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2026-08-06 | 137 | `tests/interfaces/facades/test_attestation_parity_heldout_2e16.py` |\n| 2026-08-06 | 75 | `tests/unit/metrics/test_dead_values_heldout_7504.py` |\n| 2026-08-06 | 176 | `tests/unit/test_code_review_provenance_heldout_2d1c.py` |\n| 2026-08-06 | 122 | `tests/unit/test_reviewed_tree_binding_heldout_da31.py` |\n| 2026-08-06 | 145 | `tests/unit/test_snapshot_contract_heldout_8537.py` |\n| **2026-10-20** | 116 | `tests/unit/reconciler/mutate/test_update_priority_heldout_c9c6.py` |\n\nTotal **771 LOC** across 6 modules. Measured at `origin/main` via\n`git ls-files --with-tree=origin/main | grep _heldout` and\n`git log --diff-filter=A --format=%ad --date=short -1 -- <path>`.\n\n## Why this matters beyond the 771 LOC\n\nThis is a **fail-open oracle applied to an acceptance criterion** — the same antipattern the\n`tests` code-review criterion flags in test code (`src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-tests.md`),\noccurring in an AC where no criterion looks for it. The AC's grep pattern was narrower than the\nconvention it policed, so the check passed by failing to see its subject. An AC that greps for a\nnaming convention inherits every gap in that convention's spelling.\n\nThe 2026-10-20 module is the load-bearing datum: it was added **after** the merge epic's stories\nwere created, so this is not only residue, it is an active recurrence vector. That recurrence is\nwhat story `d278-...` exists to close, and this bug is its measured evidence.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — `git ls-files --with-tree=origin/main | grep -c '_heldout'` returns `0`.\n- [ ] AC2 — Each of the 6 modules above is either merged into its non-held-out sibling or deleted,\n      with the per-module disposition recorded in a comment on this ticket before the change lands.\n- [ ] AC3 — For every module merged rather than deleted, the receiving module's test count\n      increases by at least the number of test functions removed from the held-out twin\n      (`grep -c '^def test_'` before and after, both recorded in the ticket).\n- [ ] AC4 — `make verify` is green at the change's HEAD.\n- [ ] AC5 — The replacement detection expression used in this ticket's own AC1 matches the\n      `_heldout_<quad>` form, verified by running it against the pre-change tree and observing\n      a non-zero count.\n\n## Explicitly out of scope\n\nPreventing recurrence in the `rebar-implement` workflow. That is `d278-...`; this ticket removes\nthe residue, `d278` closes the vector. Do not add a gate here.\n\n## Measurement base\n\n`origin/main` as read from worktree `.rebar/worktrees/impl-e095`. 6ed2 child stories created\n2026-09-07.","id":"d52f-823f-894e-499a","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["complexity-reduction"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"6ed2's AC1 glob cannot see the _heldout_&lt;quad&gt; naming form, so 6 held-out modules (771 LOC) survived the merge epic"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793650099506953944,"uuid":"86789d14-8fca-4c5f-ba35-d99fab6754d9"}